  "borough": "Waltham Forest",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Withdrawn",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The principle of the development\r\nis unacceptable as&nbsp;the proposed change of use to a House in Multiple\r\nOccupation (HMO) would result in the loss of a dwellinghouse below the minimum\r\nfloor area of 124sqm, &nbsp;inadequate refuse provision\r\nfor the number of dwellings and no provision for outdoor or amenity space has\r\nbeen provided contrary to Policy 20, 56, 57 and 93&nbsp;of the adopted Waltham\r\nForest Local Plan Part 1 (2024).",
    "Notwithstanding the first point\r\nof refusal, the applicant has failed to demonstrate that the proposed use is a C4\r\nor Sui Generis HMO in compliance with the statutory definition within s254 of\r\nthe Housing Act 2004.",
    "The proposed development by\r\nreason of its poor internal layout would result in an inefficient and\r\nineffective use of land, resulting in unjustified internal communal and storage\r\nareas which fail to optimise the site capacity contrary to Policy D3 of the\r\nLondon Plan (2021).",
    "The applicant has failed to enter\r\ninto a legal&nbsp;agreement (S.106) and would therefore not comply&nbsp;with\r\nPolicy 94&nbsp;of the adopted Waltham Forest Local Plan Pt 1 (2024), in\r\nrelation to the following planning obligation&nbsp;requirements. Car Free Development - the\r\ndevelopment is to be classified as car-free and residents will not be eligible\r\nfor parking permits.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nA financial contribution of\r\n£650&nbsp;towards SAMM’s mitigation measures within the special area of\r\nconservation."
  ],
